  "meta": {
    "space": "embeddings_ability.npy",
    "projection": "classical MDS + SMACOF, canonically oriented",
    "clustering": "average-linkage agglomerative on cosine distance, 2 levels",
    "cards": 95,
    "unresolved": [],
    "note": "Positions are LOCAL to this deck and are not atlas positions — the deck is re-laid-out from its own cards, which is the whole point. Anything that draws this must say so.",
    "named_by": "deck-cartographer",
    "cartographer_notes": [
      "city-4 holds 33 of 95 cards and 9 of the deck's 13 verified cards — the mass and the engine are the same place. Its four neighbourhoods split cleanly by job (answers / payoffs / draw / cheats) rather than by card type, which is why the city name has to be about threshold rather than about creatures.",
      "Aggravated Assault sits in city-4-hood-0 among the removal spells. It carries no role pattern at all (deck-facts lists six such cards), so the clustering had only its text to go on and filed the deck's entire combo plan with the answers. The membership is a measurement; read it as the map having no vocabulary for 'untap all attackers', not as a claim about what the card does.",
      "Savage Lands is the only land outside city-1 — it landed in city-4-hood-3, 'CHEATING THE COST', where nothing else is a land. It is a plain tapped tri-land and this reads as the odd member rather than an insight; the honest home is with the fixing.",
      "Miirym, Sentinel Wyrm is grouped with the four mass-protection instants in city-0-hood-1. She is a doubler, not protection — but the frame's read of her (rebuild in tokens so the wrath is survivable) is what that hood is for, so the placement is defensible about her JOB and wrong about her type. Named for the hood's four-card majority.",
      "Blasphemous Act sits in the cost-reduction hood because the taxonomy tags its own shrinking cost as ramp:cost-reduction, not because it discounts anything you cast. Same shape as the Assault case: the split is clean, the reason is not the one a reader would assume.",
      "The three Dragonstorm enchantments split three ways despite sharing an identical bounce clause — Breaching to the cheat hood, Roiling to the draw hood, Encroaching to the search city. The map read them by what they do on entry, which is the right read; a reader looking for them in one place will not find them.",
      "city-2, city-3, city-5 and city-6 each contain exactly one neighbourhood coextensive with the city. Those four are left unnamed: a neighbourhood identical to its parent cannot be narrower than it, and a synonym would be worse than the deterministic word.",
      "city-6 is three counterspells with zero verified cards and no second neighbourhood — the smallest city on the map and the whole of the deck's stack interaction. That is a real structural fact about a five-colour deck holding 16 blue sources, not a clustering artefact."
    ]
  },
